COPY public.hr_policy_documents (id, title, category, content, is_active, created_by, updated_by, created_at, updated_at, content_format) FROM stdin;
4	System Security Policy	security	Users must not share login credentials. All system actions may be audited for security and compliance.	t	\N	\N	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	html
6	Data Privacy Policy	privacy	Employee information must be handled confidentially and used only for authorized HR and business purposes.	t	\N	\N	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	html
1	Attendance Policy	attendance	Attendance Policy\n\nPurpose\nThis policy establishes the company rules and expectations regarding employee attendance, punctuality, and timekeeping to ensure operational efficiency and workplace discipline.\n\nPolicy Statement\nAll employees are required to report to work on time and complete their scheduled working hours. Proper attendance is considered an essential responsibility of every employee.\n\nGuidelines\n\nEmployees must clock in and clock out using the official attendance system.\nEmployees are expected to arrive at least five (5) minutes before the start of their scheduled shift.\nFailure to record attendance properly must be reported immediately to the immediate supervisor or HR Department.\nFrequent tardiness, undertime, or absenteeism without valid reason may result in disciplinary action.\nAbsences due to emergencies or illness must be reported to the supervisor as soon as possible before the shift starts whenever possible.\nFalsification, buddy punching, or manipulation of attendance records is strictly prohibited and may lead to suspension or termination.\n\nDisciplinary Actions\nRepeated violations of attendance rules may result in:\n\nVerbal Warning\nWritten Warning\nSuspension\nTermination, depending on the severity and frequency of violations.	t	\N	1	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 14:43:45.12829	html
2	Leave Policy	leave	Leave Policy\n\nPurpose\nThis policy provides guidelines for employees regarding leave benefits, leave application procedures, and approval processes.\n\nPolicy Statement\nEmployees are entitled to leave benefits in accordance with company rules and applicable labor laws. Leave privileges are subject to approval and available leave credits.\n\nGuidelines\n\nLeave applications must be submitted through the official leave filing process before the intended leave date whenever possible.\nEmergency leave or sick leave must be reported immediately to the supervisor or HR Department.\nApproval of leave requests depends on operational requirements, supervisor approval, and leave credit availability.\nEmployees who are absent without approved leave may be marked as unauthorized absence or AWOL.\nSupporting documents such as medical certificates may be required for extended sick leave.\nUnused leave credits shall follow company policy regarding conversion, forfeiture, or carry-over.\n\nManagement Rights\nThe company reserves the right to approve, deny, reschedule, or cancel leave requests when necessary for business operations.	t	\N	1	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 14:43:58.893662	html
3	Overtime Policy	overtime	Overtime Policy\n\nPurpose\nThis policy defines the rules and procedures governing overtime work to ensure proper authorization and compensation.\n\nPolicy Statement\nOvertime work must be necessary, properly authorized, and recorded in accordance with company procedures and labor regulations.\n\nGuidelines\n\nEmployees must obtain prior approval from their immediate supervisor before rendering overtime work.\nUnauthorized overtime may not be compensated.\nEmployees are expected to complete regular working hours efficiently before overtime is considered.\nOvertime claims must be supported by official attendance records and approved overtime forms.\nManagement reserves the right to limit or decline overtime based on operational requirements and budget considerations.\nFalsification of overtime records is strictly prohibited and subject to disciplinary action.\n\nCompensation\nApproved overtime shall be compensated based on applicable labor laws and company payroll policies.	t	\N	1	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 14:43:33.5766	html
5	Payroll Viewing Policy	payroll	<h1><strong>Purpose</strong></h1><p>This policy protects company systems, employee data, and digital resources from unauthorized access, misuse, and security threats. Policy Statement All users are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality and security of company systems and accounts. Guidelines Users must keep usernames, passwords, OTPs, and login credentials confidential at all times. Sharing accounts or allowing unauthorized access to company systems is strictly prohibited.</p><h1><br /><strong>Policy Statement</strong></h1><p>Employees must log out from shared or unattended devices. Installation of unauthorized software or access to prohibited websites using company resources is not allowed. All system activities, transactions, and access logs may be monitored and audited by authorized personnel. Any suspected security incident, phishing attempt, or unauthorized access must be reported immediately to the IT Department. Violations Security violations may result in account suspension, disciplinary action, legal liability, or termination of employment.<br /><br /></p><h1><strong>Purpose</strong></h1><p>This policy protects company systems, employee data, and digital resources from unauthorized access, misuse, and security threats. Policy Statement All users are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality and security of company systems and accounts. Guidelines Users must keep usernames, passwords, OTPs, and login credentials confidential at all times. Sharing accounts or allowing unauthorized access to company systems is strictly prohibited.</p><h1><br /><strong>Policy Statement</strong></h1><p>Employees must log out from shared or unattended devices. Installation of unauthorized software or access to prohibited websites using company resources is not allowed. All system activities, transactions, and access logs may be monitored and audited by authorized personnel. Any suspected security incident, phishing attempt, or unauthorized access must be reported immediately to the IT Department. Violations Security violations may result in account suspension, disciplinary action, legal liability, or termination of employment.</p>	t	\N	1	2026-05-26 14:27:51.442024	2026-05-26 16:15:31.0488	html
\.
